  "body": "# Associated User Story\n<br>\nAs an officer, I would like the point system to be reset each semester, and be able to edit out who is no longer a member, so I don’t have to manually set everyone’s points to 0 once a semester.\n\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n<br>\n\n\n**Officers can reset points each semester and remove people who are no longer members**\n\n- Sunny: At the end of a semester, an officer clicks \"Reset Semester\" and confirms. Every remaining member's points go to 0 and their status updates. The officer can also mark or remove members who have left, and those members no longer appear on the active roster or dashboard. Officers can still see the previous semester's totals afterward.\n\n- Rainy: The reset fails partway, or the officer clicks it by accident. Points are never left half-reset: either all members are reset or none are, and the officer sees an error and can try again. A confirmation prompt (\"This will set all points to 0\") appears before anything changes. A regular member who tries to reset points or remove members is shown \"access denied.\"\n\nDefinition of Done -\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.\n(D) Deferred:\n- `app/models/member.rb` and `app/models/point.rb` are in `.rubocop_todo.yml`'s were grandfathered in for indentation width so there is mixed 2 and 5 spacing, all tests pass. \n- Previous semester detail view is minimal. No per requirement breakdown, filtering, or search. Can change if needed.\n\n\n",
